WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.741
Sometimes a big download shouldn't take over your connection.

2
00:00:03.741 --> 00:00:07.175
That's why Arus gives you a speed limit you can control.

3
00:00:07.175 --> 00:00:09.874
Open Settings, then go to the Downloads tab.

4
00:00:09.874 --> 00:00:12.388
You'll find the Global speed limit there.

5
00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:17.233
Change it to fit the moment, like when you're in a meeting or watching a video.

6
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:21.526
The global limit is useful when several downloads are running at once.

7
00:00:21.526 --> 00:00:26.801
Arus applies the new limit to every active transfer right away, without stopping them.

8
00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:31.523
Need a different rule for one file? Open its details and set a dedicated cap.

9
00:00:31.523 --> 00:00:35.325
That cap works under the global limit, so you stay in control.

10
00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:39.802
You can also set a priority when adding a download: high, normal, or low.

11
00:00:39.802 --> 00:00:42.378
High-priority items leave the queue first.

12
00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:46.855
That way, important files finish sooner without blocking everything else.

13
00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:50.657
If you want full speed back, set the limit to a higher number.

14
00:00:50.657 --> 00:00:53.969
Try it with one large download and compare the result.

